Stock vendor VINTF manifest fragments. These are NOT copied to the device as
fragments — device.mk lists them in DEVICE_MANIFEST_FILE, and assemble_vintf
merges all of them plus ../manifest.xml into one /vendor/etc/vintf/manifest.xml.

Two mechanisms are unavailable:
  - the vendor tree, because extract-utils force-modules etc/vintf/manifest/*
    and 11 of the module names collide with the HAL libraries themselves
  - PRODUCT_COPY_FILES, because build/make/core/Makefile:72 rejects VINTF
    metadata copied that way

32 of stock's 33 are here. android.hardware.health@2.1.xml is deliberately
absent: that HAL is built from source (PRODUCT_PACKAGES android.hardware.health
@2.1-impl / -service), so its fragment comes from the source module's own
vintf_fragments. Shipping stock's copy too would declare it twice.
